{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-108594",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence is as follows:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+d,\\,{a}_{1}=___\\,,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nTo complete the formula, we need to work out the first term and common difference. The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =5(1)+8=13 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =5(2)+8=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the common difference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =18-13 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first term is ${a}_{1}=13$ and the common difference is $d=5.$ Therefore, the recursive formula is as follows:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+5,\\,{a}_{1}=13,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
